    91	The second slip was longer, and she held it a while before she opened it.
    92	
    93	"The second finding is about time," she said. "How old each piece of it is. I'm going to tell you how I dated it first, because if I don't you'll think I'm guessing, and I'm not."
    94	
    95	The words had told her least, she said. Here and there a word had been swapped for one the founding compilers would never have used, and that put the issues in order and no more. The type gave her two breaks. The stocks gave her three: a soft rag, a harder sheet, and then the bright paper of the instrument on Cael's sill, and the house's own oldest filings ran through the same three in the same sequence, so she could say which issues were older than which. None of it gave her a year. Years had come up the library stair on the Seventh-day, in Bracken's arms.
    96	
    97	"Greyvane," said Karis.
    98	
