editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:312:- Ch15: *the Quieting* — "A personal spiritual entity should not fail the way five looms fail when somebody shuts the sluice on the wheel that drives them." — *identically* — Seln: "Six sigils on the road that day," … "Five went out." … "I'm not filing that either. I'm counting it." — Karis's struck six: *one dark since fourteen; no change either side of the line; stated by him, not tested by me* — **The stratum limit, the book's only [UNBOUND]:** "It's older, I'll say once and not again, than [UNBOUND] — older than the word they retired, and I can't say by how much. Entered as a limit, not a finding. We explained the middle of the story in Ostrand. This is before the beginning, and I don't have a ruler for it." — Brom: "Say it with less." / Karis: "Everything I can date, I've dated. The floor's under all of it. I don't know how far." — "I have a hypothesis and I'm not entering it, because entering it would make it a finding, and it isn't one. It's a fear." … Lira: "Does it help? Not writing it." / "No," Karis said. "It's just correct." — "The circle's perfect," … "Perfect isn't natural. Somebody made a floor that turns Paths off. It's older than anything I can date. And it doesn't turn you off. Three facts. I'm not putting a verb between them." … "I'm not," Karis said. "I'm saying it to you. That's different."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:331:| Fractured Path predates classification (B8) | **One** [UNBOUND], as Karis's stratum limit (Ch15 equivalent); "older than anything I can date"; the identical failure is not explained | A second [UNBOUND]; any link between the floors' age and Cael's nature; Karis's hypothesis stated anywhere, including in her own window |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:356:- **C7 · Oryn's age.** "Late twenties" (Ch6, Cael's catalogue) against "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something…" (Ch13). With Kindling LOCKED at fourteen, that makes her about twenty-five. **Recommend** never stating her age. "Late twenties" stays Cael's estimate; "eleven years" stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:22:- **Cael:** nineteen (turned nineteen on the page in Book 7 Ch14, in autumn). **There is no birthday in this book.** He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure ("the Bronze from Ardenmere" in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; seal held), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used both ways), Blade (Ephram) and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted. It is the Book 2 anomaly converged, read three times, untouched since Oryn said "stop touching it". His Arbiter has been dark since his Kindling. His ribs have been quiet since the marsh. 96 marks in hand; nothing owed. Pike's sheet shows nine completed lines under the five names, and the Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The crew is **eleventh** on the wall and the season line is blank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:63:13. **KEEP — The spring (280th).** Three readers: Karis for pattern, Seln for omission, Vastin for procedure. The office's instruments. **"Behaves as device. Cannot be."** Karis stops her lamps sentence with the ruler rule. **The grade:** the same stroke and bar on all four sites, the fourth's twice the size. "Two copies of one ignorance." Vastin's three reflexes: directive, classification, "This has to go up". The second row counts a sheet short in Cael's hands. Seln sets the technician's sheet before Cael without a word. Cael does the sum (his Kindling day; five years and a hundred-some days; "six" is the office's rounding), does **not** write it down, and puts the sheet back. "You keep drafting orders." / "Habit." / "Out here the habit's the tell. Draft nothing. Just look." Cleon is named for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:69:19. **KEEP — The Deepstacks (284th).** Cleon is already reading. The sheets are laid out 11/29/12. "Older than [UNBOUND]." "I know that hand." "Being believed … It's the end of being able to be wrong." "Give me a week." Cael is unfiled for the first time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:85:35. **KEEP — The shale camp (305th).** The blanket. The rows lean along the bearing. The point is fixed. **The lamps finding** (§10). Vastin: "If a man designed the apparatus, then the sigils —" / the ruler rule. Two pages. Cael does not add his own third page (the Kindling date). **The directive and the objection**: "That's not a monolith. That's a crack." Seals unnamed. "The Compact … Yes. Part of it." The broad man's "Aye". The healers' third exchange (hands in the other's work). Seln on the pass. The fixed close (§10).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/BOOK_MAP.md:155:The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
